# Morris Ital four-door saloon, 1980-1984.
#
# The facelifted Morris Marina: black slatted grille with rectangular lamps in a
# black surround, a different bonnet pressing, and a restyled boot lid with much
# larger tail lamps. It is not a Marina, and the Marina is already in the tree.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morris_Ital
#
# Dimensions 4.340 x 1.640 x 1.420 m, wheelbase 2.440 m.
#
# Shape reference: a true broadside of a cream four-door saloon, plus matching
# front and rear three-quarters and a front detail. All four images were checked
# for the Ital grille and boot.
#
# Colours: grade (b), Morris Marina Owners Club and Ital Register colour and trim
# compilation of BL/ICI paint codes. Black, Pageant Blue, Vermillion and Silver
# Leaf are period names. Weights 13, 12, 10, 10, total 45, reflecting the Ital's
# UK volume, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 145 km/h. Comfort 60/420, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 60. Classes 1,2.
# Dates July 1980 to February 1984 (estate to August 1984), road tail staggered
# 1996-1998.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/morris-ital.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/morris-ital.dae. References: citycars/references/morris-ital/
# (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons, CC BY 2.0).
#
# Accepted deviations: the true broadside governs the body. Grille slats, lamp
# internals, badges and wheel detail are simplified at sprite scale. The Ital
# grille, bonnet pressing and larger tail lamps are modelled; it is not a Marina
# and no Marina parts are copied.


obj=citycar
